    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="1048" n="1838" xml:id="pg1838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, James C. Hagerty papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Hagerty Diary, January 28, 1954</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-01-28">January 28, 1954</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Extract]</note>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Conference in Pres. office with Knowland, Ferguson, Millikin, Bill Rogers, Adams,
                    Persons on Bricker Amendment compromise—our GOP boys on Hill still trying to
                    compromise with Bricker isolationists—George and Dems now got jump on them with
                    simple [?] George Amendment—Ferguson, Millikin scared to death of fight, keep
                    backing off as usual—Knowland inept in handling it—fine mess, all of our own,
                    because our people haven’t got the guts to lick B.A. once and for all and then
                    pass substitute Knowland amendment—best they can do now, is bi-partisan approach
                    on compromise, giving Dems credit for saving Constitution—now have to confer
                    with George, in addition to Bricker—How dumb can we get?—Pres. getting really
                    fed up with these tactics.</p>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
